From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] use L3 source and destination hash for policy route ECMP

Hash policy-route ECMP on source and destination IPv4/IPv6 addresses only.
This keeps fragmented and unfragmented packets from the same flow on the same
egress-gateway replica, at the cost of per-port load balancing.

Signed-off-by: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>
---
 northd/northd.c | 11 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/northd/northd.c b/northd/northd.c
index 1ca8dedafa..2522df5b20 100644
--- a/northd/northd.c
+++ b/northd/northd.c
@@ -11883,0 +11884,3 @@ build_ecmp_routing_policy_flows(struct lflow_table *lflows,
+        /* Hash policy-route ECMP on source and destination IP addresses.
+         * A pure L3 hash keeps fragmented and unfragmented packets from
+         * the same flow on the same egress-gateway replica. */
@@ -11885 +11888,2 @@ build_ecmp_routing_policy_flows(struct lflow_table *lflows,
-                      "; %s = select(", REG_ECMP_GROUP_ID, ecmp_group_id,
+                      "; %s = select(values=(", REG_ECMP_GROUP_ID,
+                      ecmp_group_id,
@@ -11895 +11899,2 @@ build_ecmp_routing_policy_flows(struct lflow_table *lflows,
-        ds_put_cstr(&actions, ");");
+        ds_put_cstr(&actions,
+                    "); hash_fields=\"ip_src,ip_dst,ipv6_src,ipv6_dst\");");
